  "result": "Perfect! All 117 tests pass. I've successfully added payment recording functionality:\n\n**New `src/payments.js` with two functions:**\n\n1. **`recordPayment(invoice, { amount, date })`** \u2014 Records a payment on an invoice:\n   - Only works on 'issued' or 'partially_paid' invoices (NOT_ISSUED error)\n   - Validates amount is a positive integer (AMOUNT_INVALID error)\n   - Rejects overpayments (OVERPAYMENT error)\n   - Appends payment to `invoice.payments` array\n   - Updates status:\n     - 'paid' when total payments \u2265 invoice total\n     - 'partially_paid' when amount still owed\n   - Never mutates input invoice\n\n2. **`balanceDue(invoice)`** \u2014 Calculates amount still owed:\n   - Gets invoice total from `invoiceTotals()`\n   - Sums all payments\n   - Returns `total - payments`\n   - Clamped at 0 (never negative)\n\n**Error codes:**\n- `NOT_ISSUED` \u2014 Invoice is not in a state to accept payments\n- `AMOUNT_INVALID` \u2014 Amount is not a positive integer or is zero\n- `OVERPAYMENT` \u2014 Payment exceeds the balance due\n\n**Tests added (11 new):**\n- Recording first payment and subsequent payments\n- Status transitions (issued \u2192 partially_paid \u2192 paid)\n- Multiple payments on same invoice\n- Invalid payment amounts (zero, negative, decimal)\n- Overpayment rejection\n- Balance calculations for partially paid and fully paid invoices\n- No mutation of input invoices\n\nThe payment system integrates seamlessly with the existing invoice system, respecting discounts and VAT when calculating balance due.",
